      "skill_id": "de-a1-026",
      "title": "Time expressions in main clauses",
      "explanation": "Time words such as heute, morgen, gestern, am Montag and um acht Uhr can stand in the first position or after the verb. If a time expression comes first, the subject moves behind the verb because the verb must stay in second position: Heute arbeite ich zu Hause. After the verb, the time expression usually comes before the place or direction: Ich fahre morgen nach Berlin.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Heute arbeite ich zu Hause.",
          "en": "Today I work at home."
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich fahre morgen nach Berlin.",
          "en": "I am driving to Berlin tomorrow."
        },
        {
          "de": "Am Montag lernt Anna Deutsch.",
          "en": "On Monday Anna learns German."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["GOETHE-A1"],
